<title>MALAYSIA: Unza shares surge on requotation.</title>
<headline>Unza shares surge on requotation.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Unza Holdings Bhd surged on their requotation on Wednesday, after an announcement of the company's planned divestment by Berjaya Singer Bhd.</p>
<p>At 0142 GMT, the stock was up 3.20 ringgit or 20.25 percent to 19.00 ringgit on volume of 90,000 shares traded.</p>
<p>A wholly-owned unit of appliance maker Berjaya Singer Bhd said it planned to sell off its entire 62.07 percent equity stake in Unza for 165.46 million ringgit, 18.0 ringgit a share, to investment holding firm Tanasek Emas Sdn Bhd.</p>
<p>Unza is involved in personal care and household products.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
